('128.6.b.2.B.ii',3,'Which spelling is correct for the flying mammal stressed on the third-to-last syllable?','["murcielago", "murcíelago", "murciélago", "murcielágo"]'::jsonb,2,'Esdrújulas always carry a written accent.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.B.ii',3,'Esdrújulas such as plátano are marked with an accent because:','["they end in a vowel", "they start with p", "they have two syllables", "they are stressed on the third-to-last syllable"]'::jsonb,3,'All esdrújulas carry a written accent.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.B.iii',3,'Which spelling shows a hiatus in the word for ''to laugh''?','["reír", "reir", "réir", "reiír"]'::jsonb,0,'The accent on í keeps the vowels in separate syllables.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.B.iii',3,'Which spelling shows a diphthong with no accent?','["cüento", "cuento", "cuénto", "cuentó"]'::jsonb,1,'Ue is a diphthong and needs no accent here.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.B.iv',3,'Which spelling is correct for the first-person simple past of the verb meaning ''to sing''?','["cantè", "cante", "canté", "cantê"]'::jsonb,2,'Simple past yo form of -ar verbs takes an accent.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.B.iv',4,'Which spelling is correct for ''they were eating'' in the imperfect (comer)?','["comian", "cómian", "comiàn", "comían"]'::jsonb,3,'The -ía endings carry an accent.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.C',2,'Cursive handwriting for assignments should be:','["legible, with consistent slant and spacing", "as fast as possible", "tiny and crooked", "printed only"]'::jsonb,0,'Legibility matters for assignments.','original'),
('128.6.b.2.C',2,'Writing legibly in cursive means that:','["letters touch the next line", "a reader can easily read each letter", "letters are decorated", "no one can read it"]'::jsonb,1,'Clear letters are legible.','original'),
('128.6.b.3.A',2,'A digital dictionary can show you a word''s:','["weight", "author", "syllable breaks and audio pronunciation", "price"]'::jsonb,2,'Digital resources give pronunciation and syllabication.','original'),
