('128.6.b.3.D',4,'Which idiom means ''to be extremely happy''?','["estar en la cocina", "estar en el séptimo cielo", "estar bajo tierra", "estar en el cuarto"]'::jsonb,1,'The idiom means being on cloud nine.','original'),
('128.6.b.3.E',3,'The word bat for an animal and bat for baseball are:','["homophones", "synonyms", "homographs", "antonyms"]'::jsonb,2,'They are spelled alike with different meanings.','original'),
('128.6.b.3.E',3,'Commonly confused terms such as ''a ver'' and ''haber'' differ because:','["they are the same word", "they are both nouns", "they have no meaning", "they sound alike but have different meanings"]'::jsonb,3,'Sound-alike terms need careful spelling.','original'),
('128.6.b.4',2,'Listening to a speech and then discussing it uses which skills?','["listening and speaking", "reading and tracing", "spelling and counting", "writing and drawing"]'::jsonb,0,'Language skills work together.','original'),
('128.6.b.4',2,'Why is it important to develop all four language skills?','["only one skill matters", "each skill strengthens the others", "they are unrelated", "they compete"]'::jsonb,1,'Skills grow together.','original')
