('128.6.b.6.H',3,'After reading three texts about water safety, you write one rule using ideas from all of them. You:','["copied one text", "guessed", "synthesized the information", "ignored the texts"]'::jsonb,2,'Combining sources creates new understanding.','original'),
('128.6.b.6.I',3,'A reader monitors comprehension by:','["skipping punctuation", "ignoring confusion", "reading faster", "noticing when meaning breaks down"]'::jsonb,3,'Monitoring means checking understanding.','original'),
('128.6.b.6.I',3,'Which is a fix-up strategy for a hard text?','["reread and use background knowledge", "stop at the first problem", "skip every hard word forever", "guess the ending"]'::jsonb,0,'Fix-up strategies restore meaning.','original'),
